  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Tennessee has recorded $119M in federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. The state received 329 awards with an average award size of $360K. Obligations fell 99.0% year over year. Fiscal-year totals in prior years were: FY22 $11.4B, FY23 $11.2B, FY24 $10.8B, FY25 $11B, and FY26 $12.2B. The Department of Veterans Affairs accounted for the largest share of FY2027 to date obligations with $118M. National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $1.1M and General Services Administration obligated $527K. Colleges, Universities, and Professional Schools is the largest industry by obligation with $21.9M, followed by All Other Outpatient Care Centers with $11.7M and Couriers and Express Delivery Services with $9.6M. The top vendors by obligation include VANDERBILT UNIVERSITY MEDICAL CENTER with $15.4M and FEDEX SUPPLY CHAIN DISTRIBUTION SYSTEM, INC. with $9M. Current-year totals are partial because figures are fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are buying the most in Tennessee?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer, obligating $118M in FY2027 to date. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration follows with $1.1M and the General Services Administration follows with $527K. Several cabinet agencies reported minimal or zero obligations in FY2027 to date, including Department of Education $0 and Department of Health and Human Services $0."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top vendors and industries in Tennessee federal contracting?",
        "body": "VANDERBILT UNIVERSITY MEDICAL CENTER is the top vendor with $15.4M in obligations, followed by FEDEX SUPPLY CHAIN DISTRIBUTION SYSTEM, INC. with $9M and VALOR HEALTHCARE INC with $5.8M. Colleges, Universities, and Professional Schools is the top industry with $21.9M, followed by All Other Outpatient Care Centers $11.7M and Couriers and Express Delivery Services $9.6M. Several health-related industries and logistics firms appear prominently among the top ten industries and vendors."
      }
    ]
  },
